Aerie-Purpose: Give the component updater Google's update URL while the user is opted in to Widevine, and Helium's dummy origin otherwise.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/component_updater/chrome_component_updater_configurator.cc (UpdateUrl, PingUrl)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Helium's component-updates patch sends every component update and ping to its services
origin, which Aerie turned off (services/0002), so the component updater has only the
dummy origin and the Widevine component cannot be downloaded. Both calls now go
through aerie_widevine::UpdateUrl(), which returns Google's update server while
aerie.widevine.enabled is true and the value Helium computed otherwise. Google's
server is the only one that hosts the Widevine component.

While opted in the update check also names the other components registered with the
updater (the CRLSet); it carries no profile data, and none of this happens until the
user opts in.

--- a/chrome/browser/component_updater/chrome_component_updater_configurator.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/component_updater/chrome_component_updater_configurator.cc
@@ -32,4 +32,5 @@
 #include "chrome/common/channel_info.h"
 #include "chrome/common/chrome_paths.h"
+#include "components/aerie_widevine/widevine_opt_in.h"
 #include "components/component_updater/component_updater_command_line_config_policy.h"
 #include "components/component_updater/configurator_impl.h"
@@ -186,10 +187,14 @@
 std::vector<GURL> ChromeConfigurator::UpdateUrl() const {
   DCHECK_CALLED_ON_VALID_SEQUENCE(sequence_checker_);
-  return {helium::GetComponentUpdateURL(GetProfilePrefs())};
+  return {aerie_widevine::UpdateUrl(
+      g_browser_process->local_state(),
+      helium::GetComponentUpdateURL(GetProfilePrefs()))};
 }
 
 std::vector<GURL> ChromeConfigurator::PingUrl() const {
   DCHECK_CALLED_ON_VALID_SEQUENCE(sequence_checker_);
-  return {helium::GetComponentUpdateURL(GetProfilePrefs())};
+  return {aerie_widevine::UpdateUrl(
+      g_browser_process->local_state(),
+      helium::GetComponentUpdateURL(GetProfilePrefs()))};
 }
 
